<figure id="S8.F10" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S8.F10.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.23219v1/lr-comparision-new.svg" id="S8.F10.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/118;" width="685" height="118"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S8.F10.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S8.F10.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The changes in training loss under the settings of learning rates <math id="S8.F10.sf1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e-4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.F10.sf1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e-5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e-5</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S8.F10.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.23219v1/modality_training_strategies.svg" id="S8.F10.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/118;" width="685" height="118"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S8.F10.sf2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S8.F10.sf2.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Results on <span id="S8.F10.sf2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">UBench</span> when <span id="S8.F10.sf2.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">UData</span> is divided into text data and vision data.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S8.F10.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2506.23219v1/training_component.svg" id="S8.F10.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:685/118;" width="685" height="118"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S8.F10.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="S8.F10.sf3.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Results on <span id="S8.F10.sf3.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">UBench</span> from experiments using different training components.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S8.F10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>: </span><span id="S8.F10.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a) illustrates that the training loss is smoother and lower when the learning rate is <math id="S8.F10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e-5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e-5</annotation></semantics></math> (ours) compared to <math id="S8.F10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e-4</annotation></semantics></math>(VILA). (b) ‘One stage: text’ means training with text data, ‘Two stage: text<math id="S8.F10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math>vision’ means training with text data in the first stage then vision data in the second stage, ‘One stage: text+vision’ means training with text and visual data in one stage. ‘Others’ refers to other tasks in <span id="S8.F10.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">UBench</span>. (c) ‘T’ refers to Text data, ‘V’ refers to Vision data and ‘T-LLM-Proj<math id="S8.F10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math>V-LLM-Proj’ means training text data with LLM and Projector in the first stage, later vision data with LLM and Projector.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S9" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">9 </span>Additional Detailed Results of Three Cities</h2>

<figure id="S9.T6" class="ltx_table">
